# 5. Sales & Profit Performance

## 5.1 Annual Performance

Sales and profit increased consistently throughout the four-year period.

| Year |  Sales |   Profit | YoY Sales Growth | Profit Margin |
| ---- | -----: | -------: | ---------------: | ------------: |
| 2011 | $1.38M | $248.94K |                — |        18.05% |
| 2012 | $1.68M | $307.42K |           22.01% |        18.27% |
| 2013 | $2.11M | $408.51K |           25.31% |        19.38% |
| 2014 | $2.67M | $504.17K |           26.65% |        18.88% |

### Key Finding

Sales increased from approximately **$1.38M in 2011 to $2.67M in 2014**, representing strong and consistent business growth.

The highest annual growth occurred in **2014, with sales increasing 26.65% compared with 2013**.

Profit also increased from **$248.94K in 2011 to $504.17K in 2014**.

Although profit increased, profit margin remained relatively stable around 18–19%, indicating that the business successfully grew revenue without a major deterioration in overall profitability.

### Business Interpretation

The company demonstrates a healthy growth trajectory. However, the relatively stable profit margin suggests that the increase in revenue is not accompanied by a significant structural improvement in profitability.

Therefore, future growth strategies should focus not only on increasing sales volume but also on protecting and improving margins.

