# 9. Discount & Profitability Analysis

## 9.1 Discount Group

The analysis groups transactions into three discount groups:

* Low Discount
* Medium Discount
* High Discount

| Discount Group  | Transactions |  Sales |    Profit | Profit Margin |
| --------------- | -----------: | -----: | --------: | ------------: |
| Low Discount    |       33,688 | $5.40M |    $2.11M |        39.12% |
| Medium Discount |        7,241 | $1.29M |  $152.10K |        11.78% |
| High Discount   |       10,361 | $1.15M | -$793.53K |       -68.79% |

### Key Finding

High-discount transactions generate approximately **$1.15M in sales but result in a loss of approximately $793.53K**.

This indicates that aggressive discounting has a substantial negative effect on profitability.

---

# 10. Detailed Discount Band Analysis

| Discount Band | Transactions |    Sales |    Profit | Profit Margin |
| ------------- | -----------: | -------: | --------: | ------------: |
| 0%            |       29,009 |   $4.28M |    $1.77M |        41.36% |
| 1–10%         |        4,679 |   $1.11M |  $339.77K |        30.50% |
| 11–20%        |        6,274 |   $1.05M |  $173.25K |        16.53% |
| 21–30%        |          967 | $243.10K |  -$21.16K |        -8.70% |
| 31–40%        |        3,400 | $503.46K | -$166.12K |       -33.00% |
| 41–50%        |        2,789 | $345.90K | -$214.83K |       -62.11% |
| 51–60%        |        2,028 | $168.94K | -$173.42K |      -102.65% |
| 61–70%        |        1,826 | $121.92K | -$197.48K |      -161.97% |
| >70%          |          318 |  $13.30K |  -$41.68K |      -313.47% |

### Key Finding

Profitability declines sharply as discount increases.

The analysis shows that:

* 0% discount → **41.36% margin**
* 1–10% → **30.50%**
* 11–20% → **16.53%**
* 21–30% → **-8.70%**
* > 70% → **-313.47%**

The transition from positive to negative profitability occurs around the **21–30% discount range**.

### Business Interpretation

Discounting appears to be one of the most important profitability drivers in the dataset.

While discounts can increase sales volume, excessive discounts can destroy the contribution margin of transactions.

Therefore, discount decisions should consider the underlying product margin rather than being applied uniformly.

